I see your points, but I still feel that the general intellectual laziness 
of the average person will give us a diluted version of Extropianism,
just as it has given us a diluted version of Christianity, a diluted
version of Marxism, etc. etc.  

> 
> Many positions that were once concidered hard-core are now fairly well
> accepted today. If you live on the fringes of society and refuse to move
